Description: radius-shell postinst: fall back to numeric gid for chgrp
 On emulated build hosts (qemu-user mips64el), the `chgrp users` call
 dies with SIGBUS while resolving the group name through NSS (the
 tacplus NSS module loaded by the upstream nsswitch.conf crashes under
 qemu-user emulation). A SIGBUS in the chgrp child leaves the shell
 intact, so fall back to the numeric users gid (100 on Debian) when the
 named chgrp fails. On real hardware the named chgrp succeeds and the
 fallback never runs.
Author: Agent <agent@vyos-srx.dev>
Forwarded: no (emulation-only workaround)

---
--- a/debian/vyos-radius-shell.postinst
+++ b/debian/vyos-radius-shell.postinst
@@ -9,7 +9,8 @@
     configure)
         radshell=/sbin/radius_shell
         chmod 750 $radshell
-        chgrp users $radshell
+        chgrp users $radshell || \
+            chgrp 100 $radshell # qemu-user: NSS group lookup SIGBUSes
         setcap  cap_setuid+ep $radshell
         # The users will have been created by the libnss-mapuser package
         # and possibly by an older version, so change the shells here.
